---
description: Follow the Tortoise look, screen, and accessibility conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

## 1. Look and feel

Use this shell for every new screen.

- One light theme. Do not add a dark theme, a `.dark` palette, or `class="dark"` on `<html>`.
- Inter, loaded with `next/font/google`, is the only product face for titles, navigation, and money. Money uses `formatCurrency` and `tabular-nums`.
- Use the tokens already in `frontend/app/globals.css` (`--background`, `--card`, `--foreground`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--primary`, `--success`, `--destructive`, `--transfer`, and the chart tokens). Do not invent a second palette.
- `--primary` is a mark: the active destination, a link, or the main chart stroke. It does not fill the page. A category color appears only on that category.
- Three primary destinations, in order: Home `/`, Accounts `/accounts`, Activity `/transactions`. Activity keeps that path. The phone tab bar is those three.
- Settings live in the account menu on both widths: Income, Categories, Connections, and Household. A new screen is either one of those primary destinations or a setting in that menu. It does not become a fourth tab or a second navigation.
- The shell breaks at 768px (`md`). From there up, a left sidebar sits beside the page. Under it, the same screens stack, with the tab bar and the existing safe-area padding. One component tree.
- A record or a form opens as a right-hand panel from 768px up and as a full-screen sheet under it. A top-level surface closes with the close icon on desktop and the back control on a phone. A nested step uses back at both widths.
- A choice opens as a popover from 768px up and as a bottom sheet under it. Choice lists use `Select`. Dates use `DateField`.
- The page is a flat light canvas and white cards with a 1px border. Leave out a second font, a script wordmark, wallpaper, a panel rail, an entrance animation, and a highlighter behind a number.

## 2. Building a screen

A new screen should feel like the rest of Tortoise. Match the shell above. Do not invent a new visual language for one page.

- One primary action per view. Anything else is quieter and secondary.
- One page title, then sections, then rows. The title is the only `h1`. A section title is sentence case and smaller than the page title.
- Labels, buttons, and navigation are sentence case.
- Show the next decision. Put rare or advanced choices behind a disclosure instead of stacking every control above the content.
- Put actions in the same place at both widths: the page title row for a primary page, and the panel header for a record or a form. Do not move them into a different bar on the phone.
- A save, a sync, and a destructive action each say what happened. A destructive action names the thing it will remove and asks first.
- Every view has an explicit loading state, an empty state, an error state, and a stale state when the data can be out of date. Empty copy says what is missing and offers the one action that fills it. An error says what failed and how to retry. Stale data stays visible and says that a refresh is in progress or has failed.

## 3. Accessibility

Build these in with the screen. Do not treat them as a later pass.

- Use semantic elements: `button`, `a`, `nav`, `main`, headings, `label`, and lists. A clickable `div` is not a control.
- Every control has an accessible name. A placeholder is not that name. Icon-only actions still have a name.
- The screen works from the keyboard. Tab reaches every control. Enter or Space activates it. Escape closes the open panel or popover and leaves the screen behind it in place. Focus returns to the control that opened it.
- Focus is visible on the light canvas. Do not remove the outline unless a visible replacement stays on the light background.
- Text, icons, and the accent stay readable on `#f3f2ee` and on white. Meta text is for secondary information, not for the label the user must read.
- On a phone, primary controls and tab items have a target of at least 44px.
- Color does not carry the meaning alone. Pair income, spending, transfer, and error colors with text or an icon.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Panel and sheet motion is not required to use the screen.
- A custom widget exposes its name, role, and value. A panel is a dialog. A popover names itself. A tab exposes which item is selected. A toggle uses `aria-pressed` or `aria-expanded`.
